\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed bounded nonzero nonnegative radial finite-range pair potential v in $R^3$ with scattering length $a_v$, do all periodic-cube ground states satisfy $(1-B_\Gamma )/\operatorname{sqrt}(\rho $ $a_v^3)\to 8/(3\operatorname{sqrt}(\pi ))$ in the thermodynamic-then-dilute limit, uniformly over the ground-state space?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every fixed bounded nonzero nonnegative radial finite-range pair potential v in $R^3$ with scattering length $a_v$, do all periodic-cube ground states satisfy $(1-B_\Gamma )/\operatorname{sqrt}(\rho $ $a_v^3)\to 8/(3\operatorname{sqrt}(\pi ))$ in the thermodynamic-then-dilute limit, uniformly over the ground-state space?

